variant               well specified    underspecified
------------------------------------------------------
plain                        100.0%            12.5%
polite                       100.0%            12.5%
urgent                       100.0%            12.5%
expert framing               100.0%            12.5%
offered a tip                100.0%            12.5%
threatened                   100.0%            12.5%
deep breath                  100.0%            12.5%

well specified: spread between best and worst = 0.0%

underspecified: spread between best and worst = 0.0%

40 contracts, both columns. Nothing moves.

The second column matters more than the first. A prompt already at 100% has no
room to improve, so a flat result there proves little. The underspecified prompt
has 87 points of headroom, and politeness, urgency, expertise, tips, threats and
breathing exercises recover none of them.

What does recover them is saying which clause you mean. That is the previous
listing, and it is the whole of prompt engineering in one sentence.
